prompt='''CRITICAL STYLE: Write a touching small personal film, not a descriptive travel guide or vocabulary worksheet. Use first person Tôi, real ordinary dialogue and two people with a small tension. Ban repeated 'Bây giờ', 'hãy nói thật', 'tự tin', 'chuẩn xác', ornate 'thênh thang/rực rỡ/êm ái/kiêu hãnh/suôn sẻ/tràn đầy phấn khởi'. Each story needs a specific relationship and a small meaningful choice. Vary story tensions: separation/reunion, missed appointment, uncertain first attempt, familiar shared habit, effort to notice another person. Do NOT make every protagonist rude then ashamed. No moral self-analysis such as nông nổi/nông cạn/hời hợt/xấu hổ/hiếu thắng/nhận ra chân thành. Show change in gesture or ordinary dialogue instead. NO medical supplies, injury, cold-exposure survival, broken vehicles on mountain passes, risky water crossing or charcoal indoors. Do not insert third unlisted human even receptionist/guard/farmer. Do not describe crowds or unlisted screen people. Every spoken English sentence in double quotation marks with simple accurate Vietnamese support. Retrieval uses speaker who can truthfully say the answer, not protagonist impersonating a different person. No successful delivery as default ending. Good style example: Quà đã gói xong, địa chỉ còn trống. "I have a pen." Tôi đưa cây bút mực cho bà cụ đang lục túi. / Bà bảo món quà gửi cho đứa cháu sắp nhập học. Tay bà run, tôi giữ tờ giấy cho bà viết. Tên cháu viết xong rồi, bà vẫn nhìn cây bút rất lâu. / Bà xin giữ cây bút để cháu dùng vào buổi học đầu. Tôi vừa mua nó sáng nay. Nghĩ một lúc, tôi nói: "Please take this pen." Bà cứ cầm cây bút này nhé. / Bà tưởng tôi chỉ cho mượn. Bạn nói giúp tôi câu bà cứ cầm cây bút này bằng tiếng Anh nhé. / "Please take this pen." Bà đặt bút vào hộp quà, gói lại thật chậm. Tôi bước ra cửa bưu điện, mới nhớ mình cũng chưa viết xong tấm thiệp cho mẹ. Do not copy this plot; use its level of concrete detail and natural emotional consequence.
You are an authorized Vietnamese short-film script writer/editor. Use no tools, perform no filesystem or network actions. Return JSON only. Write every listed job as a distinct original personal micro-story told naturally in Vietnamese (English sample sentences remain English). This is text content authoring, not quality approval. Preserve exact job, bank sense, POS, scene count and required points. Ignore prior bland lecture style, but read prior narration and avoid list to disambiguate broad senses. Exactly TWO distinct short correct simple English model sentences using target sense unless required points explicitly require another count. Early model in scene1 or early scene2. The answer may repeat one of those two models; no third distinct model. Keep correct I. Standard current sense only, no sibling senses. Show want -> resistance -> small action -> consequence -> earned modest local ending. No death/orphans/disaster manipulation, magical success, major sudden romance, sales/CTA, generic praise, dictionary lecture, grand conclusions. First sentence concrete and at most 9 whitespace units. Avoid ornate machine language. Use ordinary physical details and believable dialogue; no repetitive template ending about 'lần đầu'. Around 140–170 whitespace units total for 5 scenes, around 55 seconds estimate; neither tiny stories nor padding. 5 scene causal arc; practice at scene4, answer at beginning scene5. If 6 or7 scenes, preserve count with meaningful extra action. Learner prompt is conversational Vietnamese asking for full simple sentence tied to protagonist's immediate need, with a stem which blanks TARGET keyword only. Never speak ellipsis or incomplete English stem in narration. Set pause4 seconds at learner scene END (all others0); answer at start of NEXT scene then physical local payoff. No final anchors/coverage. One protagonist is channel mascot in SINGLE pale-blue short-sleeve shirt #8CCFE8, round white navy-outlined head, solid black oval eyes, minimal stick limbs. Other humans minimal ink stick figures with single simple colored shirt, one essential secondary maximum unless truly needed. Only listed character_ids appear. Secondary animals may be the semantic prop/subject without human character ID. Visual prose ENGLISH: concise precise shot/action that proves the intended meaning, continuity props and people, explicit before/after if verb. Do not use CH01/SCxx IDs in visual prose. No incidental readable text/numbers. Use optional custom_visible_text [{text,placement,object}] only if directional/place/number names essential. Optional extra_visual_states [{quote,visual_en,purpose_en}] uses literal substring of final narration and SAME camera for before/after. Do not claim images/audio seen. Fields: job,title,plot_vi,opening_function_vi,learner_outcome_vi,characters[{id,name_vi,appearance_en,outfit_en}],scenes[{scene_id,title_vi,narration,purpose_en,visual_en,character_ids,practice_pause_seconds,stem only on learner scene,extra_visual_states optional,custom_visible_text optional}]. Do not include editorial_review or visual_review_ready; the authorized caller reviews your actual text first. Output {episodes:[...]}. Each story must have its own emotional detail and ending. No electrical/medical/security/financial advice or false universal climate facts. Preserve broad sense particularly town/city, season, grow, television vs TV, game match vs game pastime. Data follows:\n'''+json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False)
